Z||000015||mshill||05-08-2001||03:39 PM||||I had a Triumph GT6 (like a Spitfire but with a straight 6 and a hard fastback).  My electrical wasn't bad, but every rubber seal had to be replaced every year.  It got expensive having to rebuild brake and clutch, master, slave and calipers every year or so.<P>The GT6 was so light in the back end that if you wanted to do any semi-serious driving you had to have a full tank of gas, the spare tire and a 150-200 lb. passenger along just to keep the front end pointed in the right direction.||||reg||1
